WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.730
JEN: Today, we're talking
about Cloud Domains, Network

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.070
Connectivity Center, and
reCaptcha Enterprise.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.050
I'm Jen, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.830
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.440
We created cloud domains
with the goal of simplifying

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.910
domain-related tasks.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.370
And we've continued to build
on that initial release

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.110
with new functionality.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.910
Cloud domains
allows you to manage

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.550
access controls for
domains through Cloud IAM

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.890
and manage your domain
registrations and renewals

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.470
through cloud billing for
a more seamless experience

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.120
with the rest of Google Cloud.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.520
Head to the blog for more
functionality and to get

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.870
started.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.630
Network Connectivity
Center-- our unified network

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.790
connectivity
management solution is

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.910
generally available in 15
regions across the US, UK,

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.390
India, Australia, and Japan.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.460
And we are en route to
expanding this coverage

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.650
to include all
Google Cloud regions,

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.320
enabling global on
ramp to the Cloud.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.500
We are committed to maintaining
an open and flexible cloud

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.650
networking environment that
will enable interconnectivity

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.080
with the Google Cloud
network, and partners

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.760
play a critical role in this.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.370
Check out the blog for details.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:10.490
ReCAPTCHA is a security
product and has always

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.640
sought to be hard on
bots and easy on humans.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.830
As bots have gotten
smarter, we needed

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.490
to adjust to keep this balance.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.660
So in this latest version
of reCAPTCHA, reCAPTCHA

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.240
Enterprise, we've created
a new detection method

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.910
that provides a frictionless
experience for users,

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.640
but is still effective
at identifying bots.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.310
To learn more about our
two primary principles,

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.610
protect users and provide a
frictionless user experience,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.437
check out the blog.

00:01:36.437 --> 00:01:38.520
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.840
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.240
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.110
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:46.820
We'll see you in the cloud.

